<title>CANADA: Draxis says FDA finds Anipryl effective.</title>
<headline>Draxis says FDA finds Anipryl effective.</headline>
<dateline>MISSISSAUGA, Ont. 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Draxis Health Inc said Thursday the U.S. Food and Drug Administration has found the drug Anipryl effective against canine Cushing's disease.</p>
<p>The company said it expects to launch Anipryl in the U.S. in the second quarter of 1997 following the FDA's review of its manufacturing file, labeling and Freedom of Information summary.</p>
<p>About 150,000 dogs in the U.S. are diagnosed with Cushing's disease every year, said the company.</p>
</text>
